WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:04.820
- [Narrator] Smoke rising through the air,

00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:06.650
and papers scattered across the ground

00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:08.173
as far as the eye can see.

00:00:09.171 --> 00:00:12.838
(speaking foreign language)

00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:16.180
This video shot by a
resident shows the aftermath

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:17.990
of an explosion at an apartment building

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:20.300
in Chernihiv, Ukraine on March 3rd.

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:22.560
At least 47 people died
in Russian bombings

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:23.783
in this city that day.

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:28.750
Many other strikes have
directly hit civilians.

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:30.810
Schools, houses, and evacuation routes

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:33.409
in the country have been
attacked and severely damaged,

00:00:33.409 --> 00:00:35.130
on top of infrastructure

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:37.163
including this children's hospital.

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:41.490
- Russia's denied targeting
civilians, but our reporting

00:00:41.490 --> 00:00:44.880
in Ukraine and videos show that in fact,

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:47.540
civilians have been badly hit.

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:48.450
- [Narrator] Journal reporters

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:51.530
and the news intelligence
agency Storyful corroborated

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:52.930
dozens of video clips shared

00:00:52.930 --> 00:00:55.440
by Ukrainian officials and residents.

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:57.670
Analysis of those videos shows that,

00:00:57.670 --> 00:00:59.330
despite the Kremlin's denials,

00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:02.100
Russian forces have been
hitting civilians across Ukraine

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:04.980
as resistance slowed
their military advances.

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:07.100
Chernihiv is a city in Northern Ukraine,

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:10.050
home to more than 280,000 people.

00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:12.960
A strategic location northeast
of Kyiv, and near the border

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:15.240
with Belarus has led to a heavy presence

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:16.983
of Russian forces in the area.

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:22.100
Near the building seen in this
footage, there's a hospital,

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:25.810
a hotel, shops, but no sign
of Ukrainian military presence

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:28.300
or facilities, apart
from a checkpoint manned

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:31.167
by a few volunteers,
according to residents.

00:01:31.167 --> 00:01:34.020
In that neighborhood, a
dash cam recording posted

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:36.973
to social media shows
the powerful explosion.

00:01:39.689 --> 00:01:42.740
(device exploding)

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:45.500
Footage shows a children's
playground after the blast,

00:01:45.500 --> 00:01:47.290
as well as the remains of a pharmacy

00:01:47.290 --> 00:01:50.210
which Google Earth images show
previously looked like this.

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:52.890
- This is a place you, you
know, go shopping, and take

00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:56.300
your kids to to go and play in
the playground a little bit.

00:01:56.300 --> 00:02:00.163
It's a very quiet,
pleasant, residential area.

00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:02.460
- [Narrator] The woman
who shot this video,

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:05.080
who is also a journalist,
told the Wall Street Journal

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:07.560
that she was shopping
when the attack happened.

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:10.640
She rushed home, where her
son was with his grandmother.

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:13.220
- Her son and his grandmother
survived, but you see,

00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:15.530
you know, they're now in
a difficult situation,

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:17.501
no gas, electricity,
everything smashed up,

00:02:17.501 --> 00:02:19.773
terrible destruction.

00:02:20.810 --> 00:02:22.580
- [Narrator] The family
managed to flee a few days

00:02:22.580 --> 00:02:23.603
after the attack.

00:02:25.210 --> 00:02:27.800
But in many cities under
siege, residents say

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:31.210
they've been trapped, and
are struggling to survive.

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:33.070
In the southern city of Mariupol,

00:02:33.070 --> 00:02:34.550
there were scenes of desperation

00:02:34.550 --> 00:02:37.979
as dead bodies could be seen
uncollected on the streets.

00:02:37.979 --> 00:02:41.646
(speaking foreign language)

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:49.670
Ukraine and Russia said more
than once that they had agreed

00:02:49.670 --> 00:02:51.084
on some logistics for
humanitarian quarters

00:02:51.084 --> 00:02:54.741
to let residents flee some
cities, including Mariupo,

00:02:54.741 --> 00:02:58.751
but efforts were complicated
by continued fighting.

00:02:58.751 --> 00:03:01.620
On March 9th, President
Volodymyr Zelenskyy was one

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:03.840
of several Ukrainian
officials to share videos

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:06.940
showing a severely damaged
children's hospital.

00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:09.430
Russia's Foreign Minister said
the hospital was being used

00:03:09.430 --> 00:03:11.490
as a base by Ukrainian fighters,

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:13.463
a claim denied by the city's mayor.

00:03:14.586 --> 00:03:18.253
(speaking foreign language)

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:28.090
Those trying to leave
have also faced attacks.

00:03:28.090 --> 00:03:29.870
According to the mayor of Irpin,

00:03:29.870 --> 00:03:31.880
at least eight civilians
were killed by shelling

00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:34.833
during an evacuation attempt
in this suburb of Kyiv.

00:03:36.790 --> 00:03:39.883
Scenes of destruction resemble
each other across Ukraine.

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:44.430
In Zhytomyr, which is located
west of Kyiv, video shows

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:47.300
a school building reduced
mostly to rubble on March 4th.

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:48.670
The footage was circulated

00:03:48.670 --> 00:03:51.440
on a telegram channel about war videos.

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:53.380
- It is something of a strange
target for the Russians

00:03:53.380 --> 00:03:55.937
in the sense that it doesn't
lie on the front lines.

00:03:55.937 --> 00:03:58.499
- And in Kharkiv, Ukraine's
second largest city,

00:03:58.499 --> 00:04:00.780
large scale destruction of residential

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:03.500
and historical buildings was
documented for several days

00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:05.960
in a row after Russian forces failed

00:04:05.960 --> 00:04:08.380
to capture major urban centers.

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:10.300
- What the locals say is
that this simply looked

00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:12.230
like a way to try to terrify them,

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:15.223
to frighten them by
indiscriminate bombing.

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:18.850
- [Narrator] Russian president
Vladmir Putin has denied

00:04:18.850 --> 00:04:21.050
that Moscow is targeting civilians.

00:04:21.050 --> 00:04:24.180
On March 7th in a phone call
with a European official,

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:26.360
Putin said his forces
were taking steps to save

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:30.580
civilian lives by offering
escape corridors for residents.

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:33.420
He also accused Kyiv of
obstructing those efforts,

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:36.460
according to the Kremlin's
account of the phone call.

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:38.752
Ukrainian President Volodymyr
Zelenskyy has repeatedly

00:04:38.752 --> 00:04:40.315
denounced the attacks.

00:04:40.315 --> 00:04:43.982
(speaking foreign language)

00:04:53.350 --> 00:04:56.100
In early March, the International
Criminal Court opened

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:59.830
an investigation into possible
war crimes in Ukraine.

00:04:59.830 --> 00:05:02.246
With bombs and missiles pounding
cities across the country,

00:05:02.246 --> 00:05:05.620
the United Nations said
hundreds of civilians had died,

00:05:05.620 --> 00:05:08.550
many more had been wounded,
and millions had fled,

00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:10.880
contributing to the
worst humanitarian crisis

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:12.473
in Europe since World War II.

00:05:13.621 --> 00:05:16.121
(light music)

